    <span class="wl-leaderboard-class">Waitlist leaderboard · production, 2021</span>
    <dl class="wl-leaderboard-list">
      <dt>Top referrer</dt><dd>Majid · 1,566 invites</dd>
      <dt>Mechanic</dt><dd>Public ranking, podium, top-ten list</dd>
      <dt>Function</dt><dd>Competition layered on skip-the-line</dd>
    </dl>
  </aside>
</section>

<!-- DIFF SLIDER — v1 vs v2 of the position screen -->
<section class="wl-diff">
  <header class="wl-diff-header">
    <span class="wl-diff-eyebrow">Design evolution</span>
    <h3 class="wl-diff-heading">Sharper hierarchy.<br/>Higher pull.</h3>
    <p class="wl-diff-desc">Drag the handle to compare v1 (2021) with v2 (2022). Same psychology underneath. The redesign tightened visual hierarchy, lifted the apex reward into view, and added education during the wait — every change was a UX-law call.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="wl-diff-stage" id="wlDiffStage">
    <!-- BEFORE (v1, 2021) -->
    <div class="wl-diff-pane wl-diff-pane--before">
      <img src="/images/Sadapay/old-waitlist.png" alt="SadaPay waitlist v1 — 2021. Uniform peach hero, text-heavy reward tiers, gray Founder's Club card preview." class="wl-diff-img" loading="lazy" />
      <span class="wl-diff-tag wl-diff-tag--before">v1 · 2021</span>
    </div>
    <!-- AFTER (v2, 2022) -->
    <div class="wl-diff-pane wl-diff-pane--after">
      <img src="/images/Sadapay/waitlist-position.png" alt="SadaPay waitlist v2 — 2022 refresh. Large typographic position number, locked reward tiers, stories carousel, Founders Club black card preview." class="wl-diff-img" loading="lazy" />
      <span class="wl-diff-tag wl-diff-tag--after">v2 · 2022</span>
    </div>
    <!-- DRAG HANDLE -->
    <div class="wl-diff-handle" role="slider" tabindex="0" aria-label="Drag to compare before and after">
      <span class="wl-diff-handle-knob" aria-hidden="true">⇆</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="wl-diff-caption">Position became typographic hierarchy. Reward tiers got lock icons and a progress tracker. A stories carousel was added for education during the wait. The Founder's Club card preview switched from gray placeholder to the actual black card.</p>
</section>

<!-- STAGE TWO -->
<section class="sub-section sub-section--editorial">
  <div class="sub-section-inner">
    <span class="sub-section-label">Stage two — Bridge</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="sub-section-heading">We didn't design<br/>golden tickets. <span class="accent">Demand did</span>.</h2>
      <div class="sub-section-body">
        <p>Soon after the pilot launched, employees fielded direct asks. <em>"Can you graduate me?"</em> Untrackable in the backend. So we shipped golden tickets — unique one-time codes distributed randomly to existing wallet users. Recipients could redeem them to bypass the waitlist entirely. Limited supply. Premium visual treatment, presented on black like a Wonka prop.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- GOLDEN TICKET REDEEM VISUAL -->
<figure class="wl-shot wl-shot--single wl-shot--dark">
  <img src="/images/Sadapay/golden-ticket-redeem.png" alt="SadaPay Golden Ticket redemption screen. Black background, large 3D gold ticket illustration with SadaPay branding, heading reads Skip the line — Get your account using a golden ticket." class="wl-shot-img" loading="lazy" />
  <figcaption class="wl-shot-caption">The Wonka moment. Black background, embossed gold, a Pakistani fintech doing premium visual design no one expected.</figcaption>
</figure>

<section class="sub-section sub-section--editorial">
  <div class="sub-section-inner">
    <span class="sub-section-label">Stage two, continued</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="sub-section-heading">Then users started<br/><span class="accent">trading them</span>.</h2>
      <div class="sub-section-body">
        <p>Recipients who'd run out of friends to invite started selling tickets on social media — first for free, then priced. YouTube tutorials appeared on how to "graduate" faster. Users started treating golden tickets like easter eggs — collectibles to share, screenshot, brag about. SadaPay had so much hidden delight built into it that users started spreading it themselves.</p>
        <p>Irfan Junejo, Pakistan's most-followed YouTube vlogger, tweeted in January 2023: <em>"Sadapay Golden Ticket. You're welcome."</em> One ticket given away to his 1.6M followers. Organic, unpaid, exactly the cultural circulation we couldn't have bought.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- GOLDEN TICKET SHARE VISUAL -->
<figure class="wl-shot wl-shot--single">
  <img src="/images/Sadapay/golden-ticket-share.png" alt="SadaPay Golden Ticket share UI. List of unique alphanumeric codes (HD7GSU8) with SHARE buttons. Heading reads Help your friends skip the SadaPay waitlist. Subtext: Remember, a code can only be redeemed once." class="wl-shot-img" loading="lazy" />
  <figcaption class="wl-shot-caption">Each ticket was a one-time code, attached to a specific recipient. Designed scarcity, not abundance.</figcaption>
</figure>

<!-- PULLQUOTE: the restraint -->
<section class="sub-pullquote sub-pullquote--wide">
  <div class="sub-pullquote-mark">&#8220;</div>
  <p class="sub-pullquote-text">We let the secondary market run. Engagement was compounding, and people paying real money for invite codes was the strongest signal possible that we'd built something with perceived value beyond utility.</p>
  <p class="sub-pullquote-cite">On the choice not to shut it down</p>
</section>

<section class="sub-section sub-section--editorial">
  <div class="sub-section-inner">
    <span class="sub-section-label">Restraint as strategy</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="sub-section-heading">One short statement.<br/>Then we <span class="accent">throttled supply</span>.</h2>
      <div class="sub-section-body">
        <p>We had two options. Shut it down or let it run. We let it run. Engagement was compounding, and a resale market for invite codes was a demand signal no dashboard could fake. We posted one short statement saying we weren't connected to the sellers, then went quiet. And we started intentionally throttling ticket supply.</p>
        <p>The Founders Club shipments included three to five physical tickets per box. The apex reward unlocked more gifting power. The system fed itself.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- OBJECT 02: Founders Club merchandise (the artifact in hand) -->
<section class="wl-specimen">
  <div class="wl-specimen-frame">
    <img src="/images/Sadapay/founders-club-merch.png" alt="SadaPay Founders Club merchandise package: laptop sticker, navy astronaut t-shirt, teal keepitsada tote bag, postcards, behavior-principle cards, sticker pack, and five physical golden tickets" class="wl-specimen-img" />
  </div>
