      <dt>Contents</dt><dd>Tee, tote, postcards, principle cards, stickers, 3–5 physical golden tickets</dd>
      <dt>Function</dt><dd>Apex reward · unlocked more gifting power</dd>
    </dl>
  </aside>
</section>

<!-- K-FACTOR / REFERRAL MATH — the system fed itself -->
<section class="wl-kfactor" aria-label="The math of compounding without paid acquisition">
  <header class="wl-kfactor-header">
    <span class="wl-kfactor-eyebrow">The math</span>
    <h3 class="wl-kfactor-heading">A loop, not a funnel.</h3>
    <p class="wl-kfactor-desc">Most growth charts narrow as users drop off. Ours widened, because each user multiplied. The Founders Club box gave 3–5 tickets back. Every redemption created a new inviter. The system fed itself.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="wl-kfactor-stages" role="presentation">
    <div class="wl-kfactor-stage">
      <span class="wl-kfactor-number">1</span>
      <span class="wl-kfactor-label">user</span>
    </div>
    <span class="wl-kfactor-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>

    <div class="wl-kfactor-stage">
      <span class="wl-kfactor-number">7</span>
      <span class="wl-kfactor-label">invites</span>
    </div>
    <span class="wl-kfactor-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>

    <div class="wl-kfactor-stage">
      <span class="wl-kfactor-number">49</span>
      <span class="wl-kfactor-label">second degree</span>
    </div>
    <span class="wl-kfactor-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>

    <div class="wl-kfactor-stage">
      <span class="wl-kfactor-number">343</span>
      <span class="wl-kfactor-label">third degree</span>
    </div>
    <span class="wl-kfactor-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>

    <div class="wl-kfactor-stage wl-kfactor-stage--terminal">
      <span class="wl-kfactor-number">2,401+</span>
      <span class="wl-kfactor-label">five rounds in</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="wl-kfactor-footnote">An illustrative loop. In production, the top referrer brought 10,000+ by the time we hit 3M signups. Pakistani fintech had never seen exponential acquisition without spend.</p>
</section>

<!-- STAGE THREE -->
<section class="sub-section sub-section--editorial">
  <div class="sub-section-inner">
    <span class="sub-section-label">Stage three — Post-launch</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="sub-section-heading">Cash.<br/>Routed back to <span class="accent">the users</span>.</h2>
      <div class="sub-section-body">
        <p>Status worked pre-launch because we had nothing else to offer. Post-launch, with users transacting, the reward unit had to switch to cash. We paid Rs. 1,000 per SadaBiz freelancer referral.</p>
        <p>The economic model was clean. SadaBiz users received dollars from international clients. Each one earned the company high revenue. Rather than spending that revenue on social ads, we routed it back to the users referring more freelancers. More invites → more SadaBiz users → more company earnings → more rewards to users. The marketing budget became the user.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<figure class="wl-shot wl-shot--single">
  <img src="/images/Sadapay/refer-freelancers.png" alt="SadaPay SadaBiz referral screen. Green illustration at top. Heading reads Refer freelancers, earn Rs. 1,000. Subtext: They join SadaBiz. You get rewarded." class="wl-shot-img" loading="lazy" />
  <figcaption class="wl-shot-caption">Post-launch, the reward unit became cash. Vertical-segmented to bias acquisition toward the higher-LTV SadaBiz freelancer cohort.</figcaption>
</figure>

<!-- OUTCOME -->
<section class="sub-section sub-section--editorial">
  <div class="sub-section-inner">
    <span class="sub-section-label">Outcome</span>
    <div>
      <h2 class="sub-section-heading">A secondary market<br/>for our <span class="accent">invite codes</span>.</h2>
      <div class="sub-section-body">
        <p>Five million users came through that funnel between 2021 and 2023, processing $1 billion a year. SadaPay sold to Papara for up to $50M in May 2024. After I left, people still introduce themselves to me with <em>"I hold a Founders Club card."</em></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

